packages) so no widening annotation can hide in a subfile.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T6","T9","project.portability"],"criteria":["E6","E2"],"decision":"dropped","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan asserts '~1770 LOC, 7 files' and 'attest/*.py' implying a flat layout, but mypy is invoked on the directory `src/rebar/attest` which recurses.","grep uses `-r` yet is given a `*.py` file glob rather than the directory, so `-r` recursion is scoped to the shell-expanded top-level files only."],"finding":"The no-widening grep oracle globs `src/rebar/attest/*.py` (top-level files only) while the mypy proving command targets the `src/rebar/attest` directory (recurses into any subpackage). If attest ever contains a subdirectory, a newly-introduced `: Any`/`-> Any` in a subfile would satisfy mypy's --disallow-untyped-defs yet escape the grep count, silently defeating the oracle's stated intent.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f00dad2c77f910f92","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, grep line: `grep -rnE ':\\s*Any\\b|->\\s*Any\\b' src/rebar/attest/*.py | wc -l`","norm_id":"n227cf3cd5bf26239","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","scenarios":["A future/existing attest subpackage (e.g. attest/backends/) — an `: Any` there passes mypy but is invisible to the grep count, so AC2 reports 2 while a widening annotation shipped."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Change the AC command to `grep -rnE ':[[:space:]]*Any\\b|->[[:space:]]*Any\\b' src/rebar/attest | wc -l` (directory, not `*.py`) to match mypy's recursion, or add a note asserting attest has no subdirectories.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiabl